B.c27=new A.Dj(B.l0,"Restricted safety, enforcement, dispute, and appeal records can remain after deletion only under the purpose-based retention, de-identification, and legal-hold rules described in the Privacy Policy. This build cannot ship until those rules are approved, implemented, and tested.",null)
B.ami=new A.ae(61355,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.c28=new A.Dj(B.ami,"Your sign-in account and account-owned profile, content, and service data will be permanently deleted. This cannot be undone.",null)
B.amf=new A.ae(61279,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.c29=new A.Dj(B.amf,"Stored-file cleanup may finish shortly afterward through a secure background cleanup job.",null)
B.c2a=new A.apX(null)
B.c1=new A.Dl(0,"minWidth")
B.bi=new A.Dl(1,"maxWidth")
B.c2=new A.Dl(2,"minHeight")
B.c3=new A.Dl(3,"maxHeight")
B.c2o=new A.dr("Store orders and visibility","Available products, descriptions, images, prices, currency, and stock status are published by the service operator. When you submit a pickup order, authorized operator staff can see its buyer and item details; you can see your own order history. Other users cannot see your orders. The app records an order request and status but does not collect or verify an in-app payment. Payment, receipt, refunds, and collection are handled at pickup under the operator\u2019s disclosed terms.")
B.c2p=new A.dr("Information we process","We process account identifiers, name, email address, account type, biography, profile and gallery photos, barber business details, including a confirmed business address, latitude and longitude, confirmation time and source, services, schedules, appointments, messages, barber, service, or location search text, reviews, replies, and likes when you use those features. For shop management, we also process shop ownership and membership relationships, join-request and approval status, private invitation-token hashes, server-recorded arrival and departure times, the shop context stamped onto eligible future appointments when they are booked, shop-customer and team-announcement channels and participants, their message content and read state, and manually entered sales and expense records. Those records can include an amount, currency, category or payment method, business date, note, the associated barber, the account that recorded or voided it, and related timestamps. For store orders, we process the buyer, selected products and quantities, product-title and price snapshots, currency, order total, status, cancellation details, and timestamps. The cart stays on your device until you submit an order. The current store is pay-at-pickup and does not collect card, bank-account, or wallet credentials. For hair-community posts, we process the author, topic, title, body, optional source link, publication and moderation status, likes, reports, reviewer decision, and timestamps. A post may voluntarily reveal health-related information about its author, so do not include sensitive details you do not want reviewed or published. For photo submissions, we also process the intended use, review status and timestamps, gallery caption and category when applicable, and any user-facing moderation decision. Our authorized reviewer records include the reviewer account identifier and display name, access status, moderation action and outcome, optional submission identifier, fixed error/status fields, timestamps, and short-lived rate counters. For content-report review and enforcement, we also process report, reviewer, case, target, takedown, and suspension identifiers; assignment and lease fields; request-audit status, fixed error fields, and timestamps; reported-content snapshots; decisions and reversals; policy basis and internal rationale; enforcement state and timestamps; and an optional appeal reference. Moderation audits do not store access tokens, passwords, signed image-preview links, or copies of image bytes. Supabase Auth processes credential inputs, including your password and, only if phone verification is already enrolled on your account, your phone number and one-time code for authentication, reauthentication, and account-deletion verification. The app keeps enrolled phone details hidden and the app and operator records do not retain or display your plaintext password or one-time code. Our authentication and hosting provider also processes IP addresses, user-agent information, and authentication or security audit events to operate and protect the service.")
B.c2r=new A.dr("Moderation and support providers","Supabase processes authentication, database, realtime, and storage data for the service. Reviewer access must be limited to trained operator staff or service providers that act only under the operator's instructions and appropriate contracts. The production roles of the trusted moderation intermediary, reviewers, and appeal or support provider are not yet confirmed. This build is not approved for release until those roles, recipients, contracts, and disclosures are finalized.")
B.c2s=new A.dr("Terms and Guidelines acceptance record","When you accept the current Terms of Service and Community Guidelines, we store your user ID, the exact version of each document, and the server-recorded acceptance time. We use this record to determine whether posting features are available and to show which rules your account accepted. You can see the current status and acceptance time in Terms & policies. The record is visible to your account and authorized service operators, not to other users. Account deletion removes this record with your account. The Privacy Policy is a notice about data handling and is not included in the agreement checkbox.")
B.c2u=new A.dr("Shop management visibility","A shop owner can see pending and approved shop members, their profile names and photos, their shop attendance sessions, and sales manually recorded for them. An approved shop barber can see their own shop membership, attendance, and recorded sales, but not the shop expense ledger or another barber\u2019s private activity. Shop expenses are visible to the owner. Join codes are stored only as one-way hashes and a plaintext code is shown to the owner only when it is created or rotated. These tools do not process payments or verify that a sale, wage, tax, or bill was paid.")
B.c2v=new A.dr("External support links","The support email button opens an external email app addressed to the configured support recipient, and the support website opens in an external browser or service. The app does not send a support email automatically. Opening the website sends the request needed to load it. Information you choose to send is processed by that external provider and recipient. The final support provider and its retention practices must be confirmed by the operator before release.")
B.c2w=new A.dr("Retention and security","We retain information while your account is active and only as long as reasonably needed to provide the service, resolve disputes, prevent fraud, or meet legal obligations. Data is transmitted over encrypted HTTPS connections and protected by access-control policies. Ending a shop membership revokes team-announcement access but does not revoke or erase an already-created owner-staff direct conversation, shop-stamped appointment, or other message record; those records remain subject to this retention rule, account deletion, and any applicable report, dispute, or legal hold. Photo-review metadata may be kept for moderation and audit purposes while the account remains active, but private submitted image bytes are removed after approval, rejection, cancellation, or account deletion. A restricted retry queue is used if storage removal cannot finish immediately. Media-moderation request audit events are normally retained for up to 180 days and media-moderation rate counters for up to 24 hours, unless an approved legal hold requires a separately controlled record. Content-moderation rate counters are currently trimmed during authorized requests, so no firm maximum is promised. Content-report request audits, decision and reversal history, takedown and suspension records, and appeal references currently have no automatic retention, deletion, or pseudonymization path, and stable references may outlive account deletion. Public release is blocked until the operator and counsel approve a purpose-based retention, legal-hold, deletion or irreversible-pseudonymization, and backup rule and that rule is implemented and tested.")
B.c2x=new A.dr("Reports and blocking","When you submit a report, we store the report target identifiers, the selected reason, any optional explanation, its moderation status and timestamps. Those report details are available to the reporting account and authorized service operators. A report action opened from a shop-customer conversation or team announcement reports the sender\u2019s account and profile; it does not attach that shop message or announcement as the reported content. The service also captures a snapshot of the reported profile or, for a supported content report, the relevant ordinary direct message, review, review reply, or gallery-item details as they existed when the report was submitted. That snapshot is available only to authorized service operators for safety review; it is not returned to the reporting account or the reported user through the app. We also store the relationship between the account that blocks and the blocked account. That relationship is available to the blocking account and authorized service operators, not to the blocked account. Blocking from a shop channel blocks the sender\u2019s account. Blocking stops new direct interaction with that account but does not cancel an appointment or end a shop membership. Leaving or removal from a shop separately ends team-announcement access, but an existing owner-staff conversation remains an ordinary direct conversation between its participants.")
B.c2y=new A.dr("Account-deletion cleanup","Account deletion removes the authentication account and account-owned product data. If uploaded-file removal cannot finish immediately, a restricted service-only cleanup record temporarily stores the former account identifier, file-storage object paths, retry count, last cleanup error, and creation and update timestamps so cleanup can be retried. Other app users cannot access this cleanup metadata, and the record is removed after file cleanup completes. Restricted service-only safety, enforcement, dispute, and appeal records can remain after account deletion in the current source. Before release, they must be limited to an approved retention and legal-hold rule and then deleted or irreversibly pseudonymized as that rule requires.")
B.c2A=new A.dr("Opening directions","When you tap Get Directions, the app includes the barber-confirmed business pin in a Google Maps route link. For a legacy profile without a pin, it uses the published shop address. It opens that link in an external app or website. Google then processes the request under its own terms and privacy practices.")
B.c2C=new A.dr("Search requests","When you search for a barber, service, or location, the app sends the search text with your authenticated request to Supabase so the service can return matching listings. The application database does not save a search-history record. The operator must confirm and disclose the production provider's request-logging and retention settings before release.")
B.c2D=new A.dr("Shop records and account deletion","Removing a barber from a shop ends the shop membership, closes any open attendance session, and revokes team-announcement access. It does not delete that barber\u2019s app account, profile, appointments, ordinary owner-staff direct conversation, or separate client messages, and it does not retroactively change which appointments were stamped to the shop. Deleting a staff account removes its membership, team-announcement participation, attendance, and barber-attributed manual sales from this shop-management feature. Deleting an owner account removes the owner\u2019s shop and its live shop access and shop-management records. Message or appointment material preserved in a restricted report, safety, dispute, or legal-hold record follows the retention and pseudonymization rules described below. This manual ledger is not an accounting archive, so the owner is responsible for keeping any records independently that law or business needs require.")
B.c2I=new A.dr("Your choices","You can edit profile information, choose which photos and community posts to submit, delete your own community submissions, cancel eligible pickup orders, report supported content or use a shop-channel safety action to report its sender\u2019s account, block users to stop new direct interaction, and request deletion of your account and account-owned data from Account settings. If your account is suspended, you may use Support to request review and provide the case reference shown in the app. Support should never ask you for a reporter identity, report evidence, or internal moderation rationale. Restricted safety and appeal records are handled only as described under Retention and security and Account-deletion cleanup.")
B.c2J=new A.dr("How information is used","Information is used to authenticate accounts, show barber profiles, return search results, coordinate bookings, deliver direct messages, shop-customer messages, and team announcements, let barbers operate shop membership, attendance, customer support, and manual business-ledger features, list products, create and manage pickup orders, publish and moderate hair-community articles and posts, display reviews, prevent abuse, provide support, and operate and secure the service. We do not use advertising or cross-app tracking in the current version.")
B.c2N=new A.dr("Hair-community visibility","Approved community posts and operator articles, including author display name, topic, text, source link, publication time, and like count, are visible to signed-in users. User submissions remain private to the author and authorized reviewers while pending or rejected. Reviewers can see submitted text and moderation details. Community-post reports are available only to the reporter and authorized reviewers as needed for safety and enforcement.")
B.c2O=new A.dr("Sharing through your device","When you tap Share profile, the app gives the operating-system share sheet the barber name, published shop location, rating, and up to three published service names. When you share an approved gallery image, it gives the share sheet the approved caption and public image URL. Nothing is sent to a destination until you select one. The selected external destination then processes the information under its own privacy practices.")
B.c2Q=new A.dr("Other sharing and visibility","Barber profiles, business details, reviews, approved community posts, and operator articles can be visible to other signed-in users. Ordinary barber-client direct messages remain limited to those participants. Legacy appointments remain limited to their client and barber; shop-stamped future appointments, shop-customer channels, and team announcements have only the additional visibility described above. Store orders, shop membership, attendance, sales, and expenses have the owner/staff visibility described above and are not shown to clients. Reports, private schedules, moderation records, and cleanup jobs are limited as described in this policy.")
B.c2R=new A.dr("Shop bookings and customer visibility","When a client creates a future appointment with a shop owner or with a barber who is approved at that shop at booking time, the service stamps that appointment with the shop relationship. Appointments created before this feature are not backfilled, and a barber\u2019s current or former membership is not used to turn earlier appointments into shop appointments. For a shop-stamped appointment, the owner\u2019s customer contact feature receives the customer\u2019s account ID and can show the display name, profile photo, most recent shop appointment time, and booked barber name. It does not show the service, appointment status, full appointment details, customer email address, phone number, private profile fields, unrelated booking history, or private barber-client messages through this feature. The owner may start a separate shop-customer channel for booking and service support. Staff cannot browse another barber\u2019s customers.")
B.c2S=new A.dr("Setting a business location","A barber can tap Use current location while at the business. The app then requests one foreground device position and uses device geocoding services to suggest an address. Nothing is added to the profile until the barber reviews and explicitly confirms the result. When the profile is saved, the address and exact business pin are linked to the account and visible to signed-in users for bookings and directions. The address, but not the exact coordinates, is also visible to anyone who has an active public booking and review poster link. The poster PDF is created on the device and passed to the operating system share sheet; the app does not upload that PDF. The app does not continuously or in the background track location.")
B.c2V=new A.dr("Shop messaging visibility","A separate shop-customer channel is visible only to that customer and the shop owner. An owner and an approved barber may also start an ordinary one-to-one direct conversation. It has the same participant visibility as other direct messages, and leaving or removal from the shop does not revoke or delete that already-created conversation. Team announcements can be posted only by the owner and are visible only to the owner and currently approved staff. Pending or rejected applicants do not receive announcements, and a barber who leaves or is removed loses access to team announcements. These features do not give the owner access to a barber\u2019s other direct conversations, including private conversations with clients.")
B.c2W=new A.dr("Photo review and visibility","Supabase provides authentication, database, realtime, and file storage services. A newly submitted profile or gallery photo is held in private storage while authorized service operators review it under the Community Guidelines. During review, it is available only to the submitting account and authorized operators and does not replace the current approved photo. Only an approved photo is decoded, resized, stripped of embedded metadata, re-encoded, and moved to a public media link. That approved link may be accessible to anyone who has it, although the app shows the photo to signed-in users. Rejected or cancelled private files are not published and are removed through the restricted cleanup workflow.")
B.c2Y=new A.dr("Report review and account restrictions","Authorized moderators may process case assignment details, the reported-content snapshot, request-audit fields, the decision and enforcement action, policy basis, internal rationale, takedown or suspension identifiers and timestamps, and any appeal reference. Full case records are restricted to authorized service operators. A suspended account receives only its active case reference and suspension time through the app; it does not receive the reporter identity or report text, evidence, internal rationale, or moderator identity.")
